    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_irony",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The irony depends on the gap between what the speaker says and what everyone in the room knows to be true."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "آیرونی به فاصله بین چیزی که گوینده می‌گه و چیزی که همه اتاق می‌دونن واقعیه وابسته‌ست."
        },
        "intent": "explain_irony",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_irony",
          "c1_humor_irony_context"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_deadpan",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The line works because it is delivered completely deadpan, as if the absurd situation were perfectly normal."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "جمله چون کاملاً خشک و جدی گفته می‌شه جواب می‌ده، انگار موقعیت عجیب کاملاً عادیه."
        },
        "intent": "explain_deadpan",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_deadpan",
          "c1_humor_irony_irony"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_sarcasm",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "Sarcasm can create solidarity among close friends, but the same wording may sound hostile when trust is weak."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "کنایه تند بین دوست‌های نزدیک می‌تونه حس همراهی بسازه، ولی همون جمله وقتی اعتماد کمه خصمانه به نظر میاد."
        },
        "intent": "evaluate_sarcasm",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_sarcasm",
          "c1_humor_irony_context"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_tease",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "Good teasing usually signals affection and leaves the other person room to respond rather than trapping them in embarrassment."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "شوخی خوب معمولاً محبت رو نشون می‌ده و به طرف فضا برای جواب می‌ده، نه اینکه توی خجالت گیرش بندازه."
        },
        "intent": "describe_teasing",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_tease",
          "c1_humor_irony_context"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_under",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Calling a complete disaster 'not our smoothest launch' is an understatement used for comic effect."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "گفتن «روان‌ترین عرضه‌مون نبود» برای یک فاجعه کامل، کم‌گویی عمدیه برای اثر طنز."
        },
        "intent": "identify_understatement",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_understatement",
          "c1_humor_irony_irony"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_punch",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Explaining the punchline usually destroys the timing, which is why humor can be difficult to translate directly."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "توضیح ضربه آخر معمولاً زمان‌بندی رو خراب می‌کنه و برای همینه ترجمه مستقیم طنز سخته."
        },
        "intent": "analyze_punchline",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_punchline",
          "c1_humor_irony_context"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_misfire",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The joke misfired because the speaker assumed shared context that half the audience did not have."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "شوخی بد از آب دراومد چون گوینده فرض کرد زمینه مشترکی هست که نصف مخاطب نداشت."
        },
        "intent": "explain_failed_humor",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_misfire",
          "c1_humor_irony_context"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_humor_irony_close",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "At C1, understanding humor often means recognizing not only the words but the relationship, timing, and implied stance behind them."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "در C1 فهم طنز اغلب یعنی فقط واژه‌ها رو نفهمیم؛ رابطه، زمان‌بندی و موضع ضمنی پشتشون رو هم تشخیص بدیم."
        },
        "intent": "summarize_humor_comprehension",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_humor_irony_irony",
          "c1_humor_irony_sarcasm",
          "c1_humor_irony_context"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_humor_irony_distancing",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-01",
        "slug": "c1-humor-irony-distancing",
        "title": "Distancing from claims",
        "rule_summary": "Use apparently, reportedly, according to, it would seem, and claims that to avoid presenting uncertain information as your own fact.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای اینکه اطلاعات نامطمئن را واقعیت قطعی خودمان نشان ندهیم از apparently، reportedly، according to، it would seem و claims that استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "According to the review, the benefits were unevenly distributed.",
            "fa": "طبق بررسی، مزایا به‌طور نابرابر توزیع شده بود."
          },
          {
            "en": "It would seem that the original estimate was too optimistic.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد برآورد اولیه بیش از حد خوش‌بینانه بوده است."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_humor_irony_register_shift",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-02",
        "slug": "c1-humor-irony-register-shift",
        "title": "Shifting register deliberately",
        "rule_summary": "Adjust vocabulary, directness, contractions, and sentence structure to move appropriately between informal, neutral, and formal contexts.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای جابه‌جایی آگاهانه بین لحن خودمانی، خنثی و رسمی، واژگان، صراحت، contraction و ساختار جمله را تغییر می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Can we move this? → Would it be possible to reschedule the meeting?",
            "fa": "می‌شه جابه‌جاش کنیم؟ → آیا امکان تغییر زمان جلسه وجود دارد؟"
          },
          {
            "en": "That's not right. → That interpretation may not fully reflect the evidence.",
            "fa": "این درست نیست. → آن تفسیر ممکن است شواهد را به‌طور کامل بازتاب ندهد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_humor_irony_reformulation",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-03",
        "slug": "c1-humor-irony-reformulation",
        "title": "Reformulation and precision",
        "rule_summary": "Use in other words, more precisely, what I mean is, or rather to refine a statement when the first wording is incomplete or misleading.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با in other words، more precisely، what I mean is و or rather جمله را اصلاح یا دقیق‌تر می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The system is inefficient—or rather, inefficient under peak demand.",
            "fa": "سیستم ناکارآمد است؛ یا دقیق‌تر بگویم، در اوج تقاضا ناکارآمد است."
          },
          {
            "en": "What I mean is that the risk is concentrated, not universal.",
            "fa": "منظورم این است که ریسک متمرکز است، نه همگانی."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_humor_irony_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-01",
        "title": "Humor, Irony & Sarcasm: part 1",
        "setting": "project review",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Noor",
          "Liam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "How would you put that more precisely?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور اون نکته رو دقیق‌تر بیان می‌کردی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "The irony depends on the gap between what the speaker says and what everyone in the room knows to be true.",
            "translation_fa": "آیرونی به فاصله بین چیزی که گوینده می‌گه و چیزی که همه اتاق می‌دونن واقعیه وابسته‌ست."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "What distinction matters most here?",
            "translation_fa": "مهم‌ترین تمایز اینجا چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "The line works because it is delivered completely deadpan, as if the absurd situation were perfectly normal.",
            "translation_fa": "جمله چون کاملاً خشک و جدی گفته می‌شه جواب می‌ده، انگار موقعیت عجیب کاملاً عادیه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_humor_irony_scene_2",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-02",
        "title": "Humor, Irony & Sarcasm: part 2",
        "setting": "quiet cafe",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Leila",
          "Adam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Leila",
            "text": "What is the practical implication of that point?",
            "translation_fa": "پیامد عملی اون نکته چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Adam",
            "text": "Sarcasm can create solidarity among close friends, but the same wording may sound hostile when trust is weak.",
            "translation_fa": "کنایه تند بین دوست‌های نزدیک می‌تونه حس همراهی بسازه، ولی همون جمله وقتی اعتماد کمه خصمانه به نظر میاد."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Leila",
            "text": "Does the evidence justify going that far?",
            "translation_fa": "آیا شواهد واقعاً چنین نتیجه‌ای رو توجیه می‌کنه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Adam",
            "text": "Good teasing usually signals affection and leaves the other person room to respond rather than trapping them in embarrassment.",
            "translation_fa": "شوخی خوب معمولاً محبت رو نشون می‌ده و به طرف فضا برای جواب می‌ده، نه اینکه توی خجالت گیرش بندازه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_humor_irony_scene_3",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-humor-irony-03",
        "title": "Humor, Irony & Sarcasm: part 3",
